From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: s6e3had: pick the display-on sequence and 96 Hz offsets by panel revision

The driver was written on a revision D panel (ID 91 10 46) and sent D's
display-on sequence and revision C's 96/48 Hz gamma offsets to every
panel. Stock handles revisions A to D (ss_panel_revision()): it takes
the revision from the third ID byte (DCh: 0x00-0x01 A, 0x42-0x44 B, 0x45
C, 0x46 D, anything else D), and for A, B and C reads VBIAS and VAINT
(C6h at 0x127 and 0x147, behind the level 2 key) to write into C6h at
0x122 and 0x142 before display on (samsung_panel_on_pre()), with A also
setting C5h, two F2h values and F7h (display_on_tx_cmds_revA; C has no
set of its own and takes B's). Revisions A and B use MTP_OFFSET_96HS_VAL_revA,
C and later _revC (ss_gm2_gamma_comp_init()).

Do the same: read DAh to DCh once after the first reset, then VBIAS and
VAINT for A to C, send that revision's display-on sequence, and add
revA's offsets (the same 18 columns as revC's are the only non-zero
ones). A revision D panel, the only one tried, gets exactly what it got
before; A to C follow stock's code and are untested.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
